| ALREADY-FIRES (d>=3.5)| windows     | 20.04   | 0.77   | 0.120        |
| ALREADY-FIRES (d>=3.5)| graph       | 11.75   | 0.81   | 0.070        |
| ALREADY-FIRES (d>=3.5)| windows95   | 27.19   | 0.36   | 0.316        |
| REJECT-PHOTO          | 1418519     | 36.84   | 0.10   | 0.164        |
| REJECT-PHOTO          | 1189261     | 98.84   | 0.003  | 0.490        |
| REJECT-PHOTO          | 1025469     | 45.45   | 0.017  | 0.172        |
| REJECT-PHOTO          | 1420710     | 32.93   | 0.0    | 0.930        |

`m3_colourfulness < 30.0` cleanly splits codec_wiki (146) from
terminal/imac_g3/imac_dark (14..21) with ~5× margin both sides.
codec_wiki is a wiki page with embedded photos/diagrams (rich colour
content); the others are monochrome/low-colour text or UI screenshots.

The 30.0 threshold safely excludes all probed photos by `is_screenshot`
gate alone (mask1x1 median << 95) — the m3 sub-check is belt-and-braces.

