## Workspace + commit

Workspace: `~/work/zen/jxl-encoder--w44-108-recover-d2d3-wins/`
Build dir (shared): `~/work/zen/jxl-encoder-shared-target`

Commit will set `dct_suppress_hint=None` default — no API-level change.
Default LossyConfig behaviour: when caller provides Rgb8/Rgba8/Bgr8/Bgra8
input, the `zenanalyze_proxies` field is populated automatically (W44-91
helper), the W44-108 gate evaluates `m3_colourfulness` on the encoder
side. For non-sRGB inputs (16-bit, linear-f32, grayscale, HDR), the
proxy stays `None` → W44-108 gate cannot fire → W44-107 behaviour
preserved.

## DO NOT

- DO NOT widen `BUTTLOOP_QF_SEED_SCALE_LOW_COLOUR_M3_MAX` above 30
  without a fresh probe sweep. The 5× margin both sides is robust
  precisely because we left headroom for natural variance.
- DO NOT lower `BUTTLOOP_QF_SEED_SCALE_SUB_MIN_DISTANCE` below 2.0.
  W44-105 already proved the gate runs unproductively at d<2 (the
  buttloop's LOW-regime tuning doesn't engage the seed scale
  beneficially).
- DO NOT remove the `is_screenshot` gate. The m3 gate alone is not
  enough — at d>=3.5 the gate already fires on ALL screenshots
  (matching W44-107); without `is_screenshot` the W44-108 sub-gate
  would also fire on grayscale photos where m3 < 30 (e.g. 1420710
  with m3=33).
- DO NOT respawn the "find a different sub-discriminator that admits
  codec_wiki at d=3" hypothesis. The W44-107 task framing
  established this is the regression target; codec_wiki's wiki-page
  layout responds poorly to the 4× seed bump in the d≈3 regime.

